{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "6f3b2b3a-1a2b-4c3d-9e4f-uyirhospital01",
		"name": "Hospital Service",
		"description": "REST API for the Uyir hospital service. Every path contains \"hospital\" per project convention. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8080.\n\nRun \"Create Hospital\" and \"Create Doctor\" first — their tests auto-populate the {{hospitalId}} / {{doctorId}} collection variables used by the rest of the requests.\n\nBooking endpoints (Emergency Bookings, Doctor Appointment Bookings) require X-User-Id / X-User-Role headers. In this deployment those are set by the gateway after AuthService validates the caller's token — this service trusts them as-is, it doesn't verify a JWT itself. Requests acting as the patient send X-User-Role: PATIENT with X-User-Id: {{patientId}}; requests acting as the hospital portal send X-User-Role: HOSPITAL with X-User-Id: {{hospitalId}} (a hospital only ever sees/reschedules its own bookings, scoped by that header, not a query param).\n\nHospital Analytics endpoints are all POST with a JSON body, called by the Admin service with X-User-Role: ADMIN or SUPER_ADMIN and a required \"district\" body field (the Admin service decides which district an admin manages). Run \"Create Analytics Snapshot\" before the snapshot detail/delete requests — it populates {{analyticsSnapshotId}}.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "hospitalId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "doctorId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "patientId", "value": "patient-001", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "emergencyBookingId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "appointmentBookingId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "adminId", "value": "admin-001", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "superAdminId", "value": "super-admin-001", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "district", "value": "Chennai", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "analyticsSnapshotId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
	],
